st suite all in place. /main.go` - full ls implementation with core + metadata/classify flags\n6. `cmd/ls/ls_test.go` - differential tests\n\nNow I'm checking the PRDs to see what pkg/format actually needs to be imported for. The ls command should get terminal width from pkg/sys, use pkg/format.Columns for layout, but implement color lookup and human-readable sizes directly in cmd/ls rather than calling those format functions.\n\nSo I definitely need pkg/format for the Columns function, and prd010-ls-extended also references it for -C mode. Let me map out what I need to build: go.mod and go.sum first, then pkg/sys with file info handling, stat operations, terminal width detection, and terminal detection. After that I'll tackle the actual ls implementation and tests.\n\nI should also account for the Linux/ARM64 environment here—the pkg/sys code will need Linux-specific stat implementations. Let me start building this out systematically.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1792,"cache_read_input_tokens":98072,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1792},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a10b715-7029-4090-909b-50ac17d5a283","uuid":"798568f7-a0b8-4643-8783-723239834fd3"}
